{"chunk_id": "b0231676fa7f", "text": "After returning from Lanka, Rama dismisses the celestial Pushpaka chariot and approaches Ayodhya with his allies. Bharata humbly restores the kingdom to him, insisting that only Rama is worthy to rule. Preparations for the coronation follow: Rama is bathed, adorned, and ceremonially installed as king with Sita beside him. Monkeys fetch sacred waters from the four seas for the rite, and sages led by Vasishtha consecrate him. Gods, Gandharvas, and Apsaras celebrate in the heavens. Rama rewards his allies generously; Sita famously gives her pearl necklace to Hanuman in gratitude for his devotion. Sugriva and Vibhishana then return to their realms. Rama\u2019s reign becomes an ideal age of justice, prosperity, and harmony lasting thousands of years. The chapter concludes by proclaiming the spiritual and worldly benefits gained by hearing or reciting Valmiki\u2019s Ramayana.\nRama returns to Ayodhya, is crowned king with divine celebration, rewards allies like Hanuman, inaugurates an ideal reign, and the text extols blessings of hearing the Ramayana.\nThemes: coronation of Rama, loyalty and reward, ideal kingship (Rama Rajya), divine approval, spiritual merit of scripture", "vector": [0.013023627921938896, -0.02628634311258793, -0.0010999685619026423, -0.00490793539211154, -0.02536984160542488, 0.00868020486086607, -0.01992395892739296, -0.00041985593270510435, -0.0314798541367054, -0.009045477025210857, 0.012777899391949177, 0.00646532466635108, -0.007464843336492777, 0.012884160503745079, -0.008547378703951836, -0.0035829918924719095, 0.043593622744083405, -0.008560661226511002, 0.01486327312886715, -0.002072091680020094, 0.008441117592155933, -0.017187735065817833, -0.026751235127449036, 0.009683043695986271, -0.013535009697079659, -0.009271282702684402, 0.012512246146798134, -0.03169237822294235, 0.032011162489652634, -0.008793107233941555, -0.014597620815038681, -0.015500839799642563, -0.0054757678881287575, 0.0138405105099082, 